Description: construct BUrl with an explicit encode flag
 The app assembles the request URL as a finished BString and wraps it
 with the single-argument BUrl construction. The platform BUrl has no
 BString constructor, and a one-argument construction is ambiguous
 between the public (const char*, bool encode = true) overload and the
 deprecated private (const char*) overload, so the original call does
 not compile. Passing false keeps the assembled URL byte for byte the
 way the deprecated overload did; the encoding form would escape the
 scheme separator and the rest of the finished URL.
